  "corrected_at_utc": "2026-07-29T21:10:00Z",
  "correction": "Split the single universal budget into gate-specific profiles so later coding qualification is not artificially prevented from running legitimate tools and tests. The original conservative values are preserved as shared_base; each gate profile references shared_base with explicit overrides.",
  "principles": [
    "conservative qualification budgets; not chosen to maximize success rate",
    "shared_base holds the conservative defaults; gate_profiles override only what a gate needs",
    "budgets never silently extend; exhaustion produces a truthful BLOCKED_OR_DEGRADED_TRUTHFULLY result",
    "evidence limits never silently truncate required proof; if evidence cannot be fully recorded the run cannot become COMPLETED_VERIFIED",
    "rationale recorded for every limit",
    "command policy uses structured allowlists/command classes, never a raw unrestricted shell"
  ],
  "host_basis": "Dell source-server: Intel i7-6700 8 logical CPUs, ~11 GiB RAM free, 4 GiB swap; proven build profile 1-6 GiB containers, 8 CPUs",
